Subject: Build fix for GCC 15 (Fedora 43): avoid std::ranges::starts_with

std::ranges::starts_with is a C++23 range algorithm that libstdc++ only
ships from GCC 16 onward. Fedora 43 stays on GCC 15 for its whole life, so
the compositor fails to build there ("'starts_with' is not a member of
'std::ranges'"). Fedora 44 (GCC 16) is unaffected.

str_view here is a lazy std::views::transform view (lowercased input), not a
std::string, so the string_view member .starts_with() is not available. Use
an equivalent expressed with std::ranges::mismatch, which is C++20 and works
on arbitrary ranges: the second range is fully consumed iff str_view starts
with it.

Upstream targets GCC 16 and considers the original valid C++23, so this is a
downstream compatibility shim. Drop this patch once Fedora 43 reaches EOL.

--- a/src/helpers/MiscFunctions.cpp	2026-07-21 00:18:49.021242466 +0300
+++ b/src/helpers/MiscFunctions.cpp	2026-07-21 00:18:49.032084614 +0300
@@ -838,7 +838,7 @@
     });
 
     return [&](auto&&... prefixes) -> bool {
-        return (... || std::ranges::starts_with(str_view, prefixes));
+        return (... || (std::ranges::mismatch(str_view, prefixes).in2 == std::ranges::end(prefixes)));
     }("true"sv, "yes"sv, "on"sv);
     // clang-format on
 }
